  "body": " Episode 7: Slope-Intercept Form, Part 2   Episode 7 Learning Goals     Given a slope and a point on a line, find the line’s equation.    Given two points on a line, find the line’s equation.      If you know the slope of a line and one point the line passes through, you can find the line’s equation.   How to Find the Equation of a Line:    Set up the slope-intercept form template .    In the template, the letter stands for the slope. Find the slope using one of the techniques or formulas from Episode 5.    Let stand for a point the line passes through. Plug into the template and the number for the slope into the template and solve for .    Plug your values of and back into the slope-intercept form template.      A line has a slope of and it passes through the point . Find the graph’s equation.  Solution: Set up the slope-intercept form template: In this problem the slope, , is given to us directly, so we don’t have to calculate it.  The point that the line passes through is . Plug the given value of m and the point into the slope-intercept template: Now let’s solve this equation for : Now, plug and back into the slope-intercept template:     A line passes through the two points and Find the equation of the line.  Solution 1: Start by using the two points to find the line’s slope:    Now plug this value of m and the point into the slope-intercept template to find : Finally, put our values of and back into the template:   Solution 2: Start by using the two points to find the line’s slope:    Now plug this value of m and the point into the slope-intercept template to find : Finally, put our values of and back into the template:     Season 9, Episode 7 Practice Problems    Find the equation of the line given a slope and a points     slope = 4, point =       slope = -5, point =       slope = 1, point =       slope = , point =       slope = 0.25, point =        Find an equation of the line given a pair of points.                                 "
